.TH "ROARK\-AGENT\-SETUP\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-agent-setup-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-agent\-setup\-create \- Set up an agent
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark agent setup create
\fIagent\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Generates flows, metrics and a run plan for the agent. Runs in the background: watch the agent.setup.completed webhook, or poll GET /v1/agent/{agentId}/setup. Refuses while another setup for the agent is running. Needs the 'simulation:create' and 'metric:create' permissions. Exploration also needs 'simulation:run', and is turned off for keys without it unless explore.enabled is set.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/agent/{agentId}/setup
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIagent\-id\fR
The agent\-id.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-industry\fR \fI<value>\fR
The industry the agent serves. One of: HEALTHCARE, FINANCIAL_SERVICES, INSURANCE, DEBT_COLLECTION, RETAIL, TRAVEL_AND_HOSPITALITY, TELECOMMUNICATIONS, TECHNOLOGY, PUBLIC_SECTOR, UTILITIES, LOGISTICS, AUTOMOTIVE, HOME_SERVICES, RESTAURANTS, EDUCATION, OTHER. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-website\-url\fR \fI<value>\fR
A page Roark reads to learn about the business. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-testing\-instructions\fR \fI<value>\fR
What you want tested, in your own words. Each scenario you describe becomes a flow. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-capabilities\fR \fI<value>\fR
The capabilities to test. Omit to let Roark work them out from the agent. One of: APPOINTMENT_BOOKING, FAQ, IDENTITY_VERIFICATION, ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT, BILLING_AND_PAYMENTS, ORDER_MANAGEMENT, TROUBLESHOOTING, CALL_ROUTING, LEAD_QUALIFICATION, COLLECTIONS, OUTBOUND_CALLING. Repeatable. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-endpoint\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
The endpoint the run plan calls. Defaults to the agent's newest endpoint. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-explore\fR \fI<value>\fR
Exploration settings Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-explore.enabled\fR
Whether Roark calls the agent to discover what it does before finishing setup. Exploration calls are billed. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-explore.max\-conversations\fR \fI<value>\fR
The most exploration calls Roark places. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-explore.max\-conversation\-minutes\fR \fI<value>\fR
The longest a single exploration call may last, in minutes. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark agent setup create <agent\-id>
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN\fR
Bearer token used when \-\-token is not given.
.TP
\fBROARK_BASE_URL\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fBROARK_ALLOW_PROJECT_BASE_URL\fR
Trusts a base URL set by a project .roark.json, like \-\-allow\-project\-base\-url.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Disables colour when set to any value.
